<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The rapid growth of digital banking has transformed how financial institutions operate, making automation, accuracy, and security essential requirements for modern banking services. Traditional manual systems are prone to delays, human errors, and security vulnerabilities, which can disrupt operations and affect customer trust. As banking services expand, there is a critical need for a reliable system that can efficiently manage customer accounts, financial transactions, user authentication, and administrative operations. The Banking Management System developed in this project aims to provide a streamlined, secure, and scalable platform for handling core banking functions such as account creation, deposits, withdrawals, balance inquiries, and transaction history management. The system is built with a focus on data security, role-based access control, and transaction integrity, ensuring that sensitive financial operations are accessible only to authorized users. Using Node.js and Express, the project implements a modern, API-driven architecture supported by secure authentication using JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\) and encrypted credentials. The design separates business logic from security layers through modular middleware, making the system maintainable, extensible, and suitable for deployment in real-world scenarios. Overall, this project demonstrates how a well-structured software engineering approach can be used to build a robust banking platform that meets contemporary standards for efficiency, reliability, and security.)
/E (The rapid growth of digital banking has transformed how financial institutions operate, making automation, accuracy, and security essential requirements for modern banking services. Traditional manual systems are prone to delays, human errors, and security vulnerabilities, which can disrupt operations and affect customer trust. As banking services expand, there is a critical need for a reliable system that can efficiently manage customer accounts, financial transactions, user authentication, and administrative operations. The Banking Management System developed in this project aims to provide a streamlined, secure, and scalable platform for handling core banking functions such as account creation, deposits, withdrawals, balance inquiries, and transaction history management. The system is built with a focus on data security, role-based access control, and transaction integrity, ensuring that sensitive financial operations are accessible only to authorized users. Using Node.js and Express, the project implements a modern, API-driven architecture supported by secure authentication using JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\) and encrypted credentials. The design separates business logic from security layers through modular middleware, making the system maintainable, extensible, and suitable for deployment in real-world scenarios. Overall, this project demonstrates how a well-structured software engineering approach can be used to build a robust banking platform that meets contemporary standards for efficiency, reliability, and security.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
