360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (In many legacy banking platforms, access control is handled using server-side sessions, requiring the server to store data for every logged-in user. This increases memory usage and makes horizontal scaling difficult. Security checks are often hardcoded inside individual functions, which scatters authorization logic across the codebase. If a developer forgets a role check in any controller, the system becomes vulnerable. The lack of centralized security management results in poor maintainability, inconsistent access control, and potential unauthorized access to sensitive financial operations.)
/E (In many legacy banking platforms, access control is handled using server-side sessions, requiring the server to store data for every logged-in user. This increases memory usage and makes horizontal scaling difficult. Security checks are often hardcoded inside individual functions, which scatters authorization logic across the codebase. If a developer forgets a role check in any controller, the system becomes vulnerable. The lack of centralized security management results in poor maintainability, inconsistent access control, and potential unauthorized access to sensitive financial operations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
